Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is "financial point of view" the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: ARTICLE 9. Evaluation of Offers. <omitted> (f) The Board may, at its discretion, evaluate any Acquisition Proposal and determine if it is a Superior Proposal. Such determination must be made in good faith and after thorough consultation with the Company's financial advisor, who shall provide a detailed report on the financial merits of the proposal. Furthermore, the Board must consider any potential legal implications and ensure compliance with regulatory requirements as advised by its legal counsel. The Board should also assess the impact of the proposal on the Company's strategic objectives and stakeholder interests. The decision must align with the Board's fiduciary responsibilities under applicable law. (Pages 88-89)\nAnswer:
